  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Mourillon beaches cover more than 40 hectares, 19 of them dedicated to swimming, with four coves (Lido, Mistral, de la Source, des Pins) and the Tabarly cove devoted to water sports, where swimming is prohibited (city of Toulon). The site has more than 1,300 free parking spaces; the Henri-Fabre promenade is a pedestrian zone where non-motorised bikes and scooters move at walking pace (6 km/h maximum).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The latest order published by the city of Toulon (order AR/PM/2026/02, dated 28 September 2026) allows leashed pets, notably dogs, to move around year-round on the public Mourillon beaches site, except on the sand, the beaches and the Plaine des Sports. The toulon.fr page "Les plages toulonnaises" adds that dogs are banned on the lawns. Category 1 and 2 dogs must also be muzzled.</p>
      <p>Two types of dog areas complete the setup: two "dog parks" between the car park and the beaches (one for small dogs, the other for larger ones, according to the city) and a year-round "dog beach" on the peninsula by the Tabarly cove, with a pontoon for getting into the water.</p>
      <p>The "Mourillon beaches rules" page on toulon.fr (article 14) repeats the same rule. The Provence Méditerranée tourist office (listing updated 02/08/2026) still shows an older version: leash on the Henri-Fabre promenade from 1 September to 31 May, and only between 6am and 8:30am from 1 June to 31 August. The city nevertheless announced on 11 June 2026 that leashed dogs are allowed year-round on the promenade, and the mayor adds that dogs remain banned on the sand for hygiene reasons: this is the rule of the order of 28 September 2026, the only version used here. Guide and assistance dogs are not covered by this article.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the rules were changed in 2025 and twice in 2026 — a glance at the signage at the site entrance remains the best guarantee. The city also asks that no soap or shampoo be used in the showers.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>To let your dog run or swim, see the <a href="/en/fiche-anse-tabarly-toulon">Tabarly cove dog beach</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-pipady-toulon">Pipady dog beach</a>, at the foot of the Tour Royale. On site, the rules are posted at the beach entrances.</p>
    </div>

